Open borders is a very broad definition. What's your particular definition of it? I spoke to one person a while back on here who was literally open borders to the max, ie no borders for any country anywhere. People should be free to immigrate where they want when they want and no one should try to stop them. Of course, he had other very, very idealistic views on the world that I doubt would ever be attainable but that is what he legitimately thought.

&amp;#x200B;

That being said, the problem with open borders as a solution is that if you require any type of background check or clearance to pass, you now have a border. I'm against the wall, to be frank, despite voting for Trump. Personally, what I'd like to see is some form of workplace verification overhaul, ie e-verify  everywhere or something to that extent and actually make harsh punishments for employing workers. The workplace raids are curing the symptoms but not the underlying cause, that is the inherent draw of illegal aliens due to work. HR staff, execs and anyone who is knowingly in on the scheme should be jailed and fined. Businesses that are found to have over a certain amount, say 50 to 100 or so illegal Aliens are clearly knowingly hiring at that point and should automatically lose their business license / right to do business on top of being jailed and fined. 

&amp;#x200B;

After that, you wouldn't need to worry so much because without the means to sustain themselves they would self deport. It also doesn't help that states like CA want to shelter them which only encourages illegal immigration to begin with. I'm sure there are other ways to handle it, but that would be my suggestions.

Level 61 Archer here on BDO with a 60 Musa. The problem with BDO is a few things. First off, the time to kill is stupid low. You go AP or that's it. DP memes exist but largely everyone goes AP. That means that everyone goes for the same set which creates a market that only exists for one set of armor. Other armor sets do sell but only for newbies leveling. There are a ton of armor sets that are flat out useless. I'm lookin at you, Rocaba, Lemoria, etc.

&amp;#x200B;

Pair that with the fact there is 0 way to escape CC once you screw up, it makes for a bad time. The combat is fun at first and the skills are flashy but if they would fix the core problem of AP &gt; all and have an actual CC escape on a 15-20 second cooldown (because let's be hoenst, cooldowns in BDO is stupid fast) it'd be better.

&amp;#x200B;

A lot of the problem with current gen MMOs is they want to focus on instances and not use the open world. That's the problem and what makes Archeage so good in it's design, though I don't like it's tab target combat. The fact the open world encourages people to do things and gives a reason for conflict is amazing. TERA used to do that with crafting..Then they removed all the pvp and crafting and made the gear treadmill. \[sigh\] Sad times, really.

