I'm a fairly dogmatic individual. These people are referred to as illegal aliens in our laws. That is how I refer to them. Frankly, the laws are simple. They are to be deported after having whatever hearings are necessary. There is already a pathway to citizenship that exists. If it needs reformation, then so be it. Have it reformed. That's what congress does.

&amp;#x200B;

However, I believe we have laws and we should enforce those laws as necessary. The only bias I have is this wishy washy stuff. So what if they get scared to act as witnesses. They shouldn't be here in the first place. Illegal aliens, are by definition, here illegally. They themselves are not illegal however their presence without the proper documentation, is, in and of itself, illegal, thus the term illegal alien. Ie, someone who is here ilegally and is an alien. It really is that simple. I care not if they are Irish,  Hispanic, Asian, Indian or what they are. I don't care if they are on an overstayed visa or if they snuck across the border. Give them their due process and, if necessary, ship them home.

&amp;#x200B;

Frankly, we need to crack down on this stuff and stop encouraging them to come here illegally in the first place. Businesses should be heavily fined, and after a certain point, shut down entirely / lose their license to do business. We should have systems put in place to make it harder to commit identity theft, things like E-verify are a start. The majority of illegal aliens commit multiple crimes via identity theft, tax fraud and the like. These are not victimless crimes as it can take the person whose identity has been stolen months, if not years to repair the damage done.

&amp;#x200B;

The law should be enforced until it is changed. To me, it is that simple.
